    "lawCode": "Amd §4.07, Arts & Cul L",
    "lawSection": "Arts and Cultural Affairs Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4722A\n\nSPONSOR: FAHY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the arts and cultural affairs law, in relation to renam-\ning agency building one, agency building two, agency building three and\nagency building four, located at the empire state plaza\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo rename agency buildings one through four at the Empire state plaza.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new subdivision 12 to section 4.07 of the arts and\ncultural affairs law to provide a process for renaming agency building\none through four on the Empire State plaza. Section 2 is the effective\ndate which is one hundred and eight days after enactment.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Governor Nelson A. Rockefeller Empire State Plaza is one of the most\nspectacular capital centers in the country. It contains major buildings\nlike the Egg Performance Center, Cultural Education Center as well as\noffice space for thousands of state employees Many of the Plaza build-\nings are named after famous people including Erastus Corning, the long-\nest tenured mayor of any large city the United States (Corning Tower)\nand Robert Abrams , a long time State Attorney General, (The Robert\nAbrams Building for Law and Justice ). The four building that house\nthousands of state employees are named 1,2,3, and 4. The naming of\nbuilding simple numbers misses a great opportunity to educate New York-\ners. This legislation honors New York's most significant natural\nresource, its famous rivers. The founding of the state is directly\nlinked to the Hudson River and other rivers have served as economic\ndrivers of the country.\n\nThis bill sets up a process for the selection of the names by using an\nexisting Commission. The Commission will recommend river designations to\nthe Governor. She will be the ultimate decision maker. New Yorkers who\nvisit will be reminded of the great natural resources of the Empire\nState.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS8722 of 2023-24, referred to cultural affairs, tourism, parks and\nrecreation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nOne hundred and eighty days after enactment.\n",
